    shortAnswerHi: 'Streams data ko chunks mein backpressure ke saath process karte hain, isliye input kitna bhi bada ho memory constant rehti hai.',
    detailedAnswer: 'readFile on a 2 GB file allocates 2 GB and can exhaust the heap; a stream reads roughly 64 KB at a time. Backpressure is the real mechanism: write() returns false when the destination cannot keep up, telling the source to pause, which prevents an unbounded buffer from forming. pipeline() applies backpressure, propagates errors and destroys every stream in the chain, which .pipe() does not — using .pipe() is how you end up leaking file descriptors on failure.',
