    detailedAnswer: 'Indexes cost storage and slow down INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. A composite index follows the leftmost-prefix rule: an index on (user_id, created_at) serves queries filtering on user_id, or on user_id and created_at, but not created_at alone. Indexes are also silently bypassed when you wrap the column in a function, use a leading wildcard in LIKE, or force an implicit type cast. Always confirm with EXPLAIN ANALYZE rather than assuming — a sequential scan on a large hot table is the signal to investigate.',
