    detailedAnswer: 'populate is a $lookup in Mongoose clothing: convenient, but it is an extra round trip, and calling it per item in a loop is exactly the N+1 pattern people complain about in SQL ORMs. Two other Mongoose traps are worth knowing. findOneAndUpdate skips save middleware and validators by default, so a pre("save") password-hashing hook silently does not run on the update path — pass runValidators or route writes through save(). And .lean() returns plain objects instead of full Mongoose documents, which is significantly faster for read-only endpoints where you never call .save().',
